  \includegraphics[width=0.90\textwidth]{FIGURE_M1_SPATIAL_CONVERGENCE.png}
  \caption{Spatial mesh convergence for Mode-I fracture: (top) global reaction force--displacement curves across 5 mesh resolutions ($h=0.00300 \to 0.00100\,\mathrm{mm}$); (bottom) asymptotic convergence of peak reaction force $F_{\max}$ and invariance of initial stiffness $K_0$.}
  \label{fig:m1_spatial_convergence}
\end{figure}

\subsection{Temporal Increment Convergence}
The influence of time incrementation during crack initiation and propagation was investigated across three temporal schedules ($T_1$: coarse $\Delta t = 0.0010\,\mathrm{s}$, $T_2$: nominal $\Delta t = 0.0005\,\mathrm{s}$, $T_3$: fine $\Delta t = 0.00025\,\mathrm{s}$) on the baseline 15,192-element model (Table~\ref{tab:temporal_convergence_matrix}).

\begin{table}[htbp]
\centering
\caption{Mode-I temporal increment convergence on the 15,192-element mesh.}
\label{tab:temporal_convergence_matrix}
\small
\begin{tabular}{llrrrrr}
\toprule
Schedule & Scaling & Base $\Delta t_0$ [s] & Total frames & $K_0$ [kN/mm] & $F_{\max}$ [kN] & $u(F_{\max})$ [$\mu$m] \\
\midrule
$T_1$ (Coarse) & $2.0\times$ nominal & $0.00100$ & $3{,}502$ & $137.95$ & $0.7582$ & $5.864$ \\
$T_2$ (Nominal) & $1.0\times$ nominal & $0.00050$ & $7{,}002$ & $137.95$ & $0.7578$ & $5.857$ \\
$T_3$ (Fine) & $0.5\times$ nominal & $0.00025$ & $14{,}002$ & $137.95$ & $0.7571$ & $5.855$ \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

The temporal variation between coarse, nominal, and fine schedules is $<0.09\%$ in $F_{\max}$, demonstrating that the nominal incrementation $\Delta t = 0.0005\,\mathrm{s}$ resolves the phase-field evolution time scales with high precision.

