\paragraph{Lineage distinction between sensitivity study and production batch.}
The counts in Table~\ref{tab:adaptive_convergence_matrix} ($17{,}687$, $8{,}120$, $4{,}356$ finite elements) reflect the historically preserved offline adaptive parameter sensitivity study. When the production batch meshes were independently regenerated for HPC convergence benchmarking, subtle meshing variation produced actual finite element counts of $15{,}396$ (for $\eta=2\%$), $7{,}633$ (for $\eta=3\%$), and $4{,}194$ (for $\eta=5\%$). Both lineages demonstrate consistent refinement trends and are rigorously distinguished in the active production matrix in Chapter~\ref{ch:current_status}.

